WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.089
Loop X two point zero. A workbench for
long-horizon research.

2
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.189
Carry the goal, constraints, and return
route.

3
00:00:10.369 --> 00:00:12.440
Let the existing owner adopt the work.

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.602
Keep corrections on the task. Return the
evidence.

5
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.315
Peers accept separate scopes. The build uses
the research artifact.

6
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.287
See work, waiting decisions, and schedules.

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.171
Separate the next task from a pending
approval.

8
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.667
Keep owners and waiting work visible.

9
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.723
Keep questions, findings, and changes of
direction.

10
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.046
Read six process judgments. Keep unknowns
visible.

11
00:00:46.226 --> 00:00:49.872
Trace claims to their source. Measure
results and costs separately.

12
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.877
One generated-graph probe improved from
forty one point two to eighty five percent.

13
00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:00.062
That result applies to the duplication
condition shown.

14
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.099
The independent control kept its accuracy.
Time rose thirty two percent.

15
00:01:05.279 --> 00:01:07.236
Native score gain remains unproven.

16
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.091
Keep failed paths and their reasons. Choose
the next test.

17
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.359
Check continuation, hosts, and channels.

18
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.163
Your runtime brings the models and tools.

19
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.033
Loop X. Keep the research, evidence, and
next decision together.
